WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.534
-You look gorgeous.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.734
-Thank you very much.
-I love having you here.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.968
You know, we were both --
We attended the Met Gala...

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.367
-We did.
-...the same night.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:11.467
I didn't get a chance to see
you, but I did see the pictures.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.868
Look at this.
-Oh. Thank you.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.868
-Look at this. Gorgeous.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:16.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.133
Stunning.
-Didn't see you.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.968
I did see Seth Meyers.
-You saw Seth? Oh, yeah?

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.000
Who else did you hang --
Who sat at your table?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.567
-I was on a table with

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:27.701
Kourtney Kardashian
and Travis Barker.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.300
-Oh, they're fun!
-Yeah.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.834
-I love them.
-It was -- Well, it was --

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.434
I needed to, like, have an in
to the conversation,

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.534
have something to say,
something interesting for them

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.968
to, you know, to know.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:43.133
But they did dress up as
Sid and Nancy for Halloween

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.834
two years ago, a year ago.
So, then my thought was,

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.567
"I'm in a show and Sid and Nancy
are in that show.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.367
And I'm in it, too, and so hi."

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.133
-"I can relate to you!
We're the same people!"

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:55.200
-And they were like, "Great!
We can't wait to watch it."

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.801
And then, that was it.
We were best friends.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:58.300
-They're fun, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.501
I do want to talk about
"Pistol,"

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:02.901
The new Sex Pistols thing.
I do want to talk about it.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.434
When you're at those Met Galas,

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:07.801
do you get star struck by
anyone, or not really?

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.033
-I do, but I really
try to play it cool.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.767
I try to not overdo it.
You know?

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.334
Although sometimes
that doesn't go quite so well.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:23.067
Because one time I was at a U2
concert and Bono was backstage,

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.434
and everyone was
gonna go and say hi to Bono.

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:29.934
And I didn't want to be like,
"Hi. I'm Maisie.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:32.367
I know who you are."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:34.334
But then I just ended up
being like,

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:36.200
"Hi. I'm Maisie.
What's your name?"

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.367
-To Bono?
-To Bono.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.567
[ Laughter ]
-At a U2 concert.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:45.133
-Yeah, and he was just like,
"What are you doing?"

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.434
I played it too cool.
-That's actually way too cool.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.501
He probably liked that. Yeah,
he's like, "What's my name?"

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:50.901
[ Laughter ]
At a U2 concert.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.434
"Well, I'm Bono.
Nice to meet you."

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.868
-Yeah, it was so weird.
-You were trending on Twitter

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:57.701
recently because they just
announced this new video game,

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.734
called "MultiVersus."
-Yes.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:04.000
And Arya Stark is in it.
-Yes.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:09.133
-You are in the --
You love video games.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.234
-I do love video games.
-What does this feel like?

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.367
You're in this game.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:14.734
-I felt woefully underprepared,
actually.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.234
'Cause when I went there,
I thought it was gonna be

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:19.934
kind of like a quest-style game,

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:21.701
and it was gonna be, like,
young warrior.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.467
-RPG thing, yes.
-Yeah, yeah, you need to --

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:28.434
And then it was actually just
this battle game,

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.701
and I had to do all these lines
where I'm, like,

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.901
cussing out
other cartoon characters.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.701
Like,
"What's up, Bugs Bunny?"

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.267
And it was, like,
kind of wild, so...

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.133
-I want to talk about
your new show, series, "Pistol."

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.434
-Yes.
-This is the story of how

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:45.601
the Sex Pistols formed.
-It is.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:49.000
Now, you play Jordan,
who is a punk icon,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.968
very close with the band.

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:56.067
Here's a photo of you as Jordan
and the real Jordan split.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.868
Look at that.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.067
Yeah, super cool.
-Oh!

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.067
-Well done.
It fits good.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.100
It fits perfect.
-Yes.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.601
-And the real Jordan passed
away, sadly, last month,

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.567
but you got to meet her
and talk with her.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.367
-I did.
Yeah, Jordan was a consultant

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:16.601
on the show, and she sculpted
everything with my image,

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:20.100
but also kind of
a lot of different teams,

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.334
you know,
with everyone's costume,

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:24.100
everyone's hair and makeup,
and she was there.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.701
-And how was she?
Just cool, right?

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.400
-Yeah, just incredible.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.868
It's, you know, quite
intimidating to be around her.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:34.767
But to be around someone who's
just so sure of themself and,

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:38.934
you know, just remembers
this time with such --

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.968
just such a good perspective,

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.701
it was just
a benefit to all of us.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.968
And I feel really,
really grateful to have

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.334
gotten to spend
some time with her.

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:49.934
-Here's a picture of you
and the real Jordan.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.167
-Yeah.
-That's fantastic.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:56.067
Man, she had good style, huh?
-Yeah.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.734
-The Sex Pistols --

00:03:57.734 --> 00:04:00.801
If you love music,
you know the Sex Pistols.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.400
I know a little bit
of the story,

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.534
but I always want to know more.
-Yes.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:08.267
-Has it changed the way
you think of music now?

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.167
-Definitely.
I think the --

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.033
You know, we shot
this during COVID,

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:14.934
and we basically
got to go and watch live gigs

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.400
every day because the boys
who are playing the Pistols,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.601
they learn all their
instruments, all of the songs,

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.300
and played live
every single day.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.234
And for me, that's, like,
how the Pistols

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.934
are supposed to be experienced,
you know?

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:28.434
Like, that was the way
that they really shine.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.934
And my experience sort of
listening to music

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:34.200
is, like, much more on radio,
or it's people's music videos,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.234
or it's their image
on social media.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.400
-Some songs are made for radio.
-Right, exactly.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:42.734
And so I think it's kind of --
Like, I've been really intrigued

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.367
to figure out what artists
I need to watch live

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.968
and what artists, like, are
better on your headphones

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.701
or, like, whatever.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:53.234
-So, I think I appreciate
the live performance a lot more.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:55.100
And I'm kind of, like,
seeking out those artists

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.267
'cause they're harder
to come by now.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.968
-I'm excited about this one.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.801
Here's Maisie Williams
in "Pistol."

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.534
Take a look at this.

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:05.601
-You've got nothing.
You know nothing.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.033
And if you stay here,
you'll become nothing.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:11.667
-You think we're just stupid
little girls, but we're punks.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:15.167
You're just old.
-Old? Well...

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:18.534
-We're the new generation gap.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.400
-Good for you.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.367
And how long before you're
the old "new" generation gap?

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:26.901
What will you have then
but to trade boring stories

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:29.067
about how you were once
the brightest young things

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:32.934
at some gig
no one even remembers?

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:36.033
Go home.
Learn things.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:39.767
Get clever.
Make your own destiny.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.067
-Yeah.
Get clever!

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.234
Maisie Williams!
All six episodes of "Pistol"

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.634
begin streaming May 31st
on Hulu.

